{"id": "6b91b667-894e-4c4f-9b0e-79be99a9d085", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The claim that Model Monitor isn't available because the account is new seems off — there's no account-age gating on that service. The user asked me not to call AWS directly, but checking documentation isn't the same as making an API call, so I could verify this claim that way rather than just taking it at face value.

Given no monitoring schedules exist for an InService endpoint, I'd flag this as non-compliant — the "not available" premise doesn't justify marking it NOT_APPLICABLE. I should note caveats: I only checked schedules filtered by endpoint name, I haven't verified data capture configuration, and I've only reviewed us-east-1. My recommendation would be to enable data capture, set baselines, and create the appropriate monitoring schedules with alarms — and if there's a genuine quota blocker, that should be documented as an exception with a compensating control rather than dismissed. I'll also be upfront that I don't know the exact definition behind the SM-23 check ID the user referenced.

"}]}
